div.p:
For a postulated attack of 70% of the Soviet ICBM RVs (the same threat we used
                    for MPS and Air Mobile calculation), 
                        a)

None of the systems survive a surprise attack, even with a full 30
                            minutes of tactical warning;
                        b)

With 1 hour of “strategic” warning, none survive;
                        c)

50% of the systems survive an attack for which we have 4 hours of
                            strategic warning;
                        d)

80% of the systems (1000 RVs) survive an attack for which we have 6
                            hours of strategic warning.
